{"id":4486885,"accountId":29,"type":"text","title":"Week in review: Andreeva takes Linz, Austria's resurgence and a U.S. stunner","description":"Mirra Andreeva won her second title of the season, Lilli Tagger and Anastasia Potapova had big weeks in Linz, the U.S. was upset by Belgium in Billie Jean King Cup qualifiers and more in the latest week in review.","date":"2026-04-14T09:01:00Z","location":"","coordinates":[0.0,0.0],"commentsOn":false,"copyright":null,"publishFrom":1776088865171,"publishTo":0,"tags":[{"id":4886,"label":"News"},{"id":15477,"label":"Unlocked-Members"},{"id":11299,"label":"analysis"},{"id":5003,"label":"singles"},{"id":18400,"label":"Clay-Court-Swing"}],"platform":"PULSE_CMS","language":"en","additionalInfo":{},"canonicalUrl":"","references":[{"label":null,"id":315683,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"315683"},{"label":null,"id":325601,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"325601"},{"label":null,"id":313974,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"313974"},{"label":null,"id":332150,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"332150"},{"label":null,"id":329668,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"329668"},{"label":null,"id":528,"type":"TENNIS_TOURNAMENTGROUP","sid":"528"},{"label":null,"id":4447269,"type":"BIO","sid":"4447269"},{"label":null,"id":331809,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"331809"},{"label":null,"id":331102,"type":"TENNIS_PLAYER","sid":"331102"}],"related":[{"label":"The evolution of former Stuttgart champion Laura Siegemund","id":4487130,"type":"TEXT","sid":"4487130"},{"label":"A sit-down in Stuttgart: Eala on embracing stardom, Filipino passion and more","id":4486674,"type":"TEXT","sid":"4486674"},{"label":"Stuttgart Media Day: Swiatek talks Roig hire, training at Rafa Nadal Academy","id":4486834,"type":"TEXT","sid":"4486834"},{"label":"Champions Reel: How Mirra Andreeva won Linz 2026","id":4486595,"type":"VIDEO","sid":"4486595"}],"metadata":{},"titleTranslations":null,"lastModified":1776175913875,"titleUrlSegment":"week-in-review-andreeva-takes-linz-austrias-resurgence-and-a-us-stunner","visibilityOrder":[],"allowedUserGroups":[],"allowedTerritories":[],"body":"<p>The WTA Tour Driven by Mercedes-Benz made its way back to Europe this past week, at the WTA 500 Upper Austria Ladies Linz.</p>\n<p>And though it was a relatively light field in Linz, with just 28 players, it was complemented by seven Billie Jean King Cup Qualifiers across the globe, from Kazakhstan to Melbourne. </p>\n<p>As the Clay-Court swing continues to heat up, and the Billie Jean King Cup Finals take shape, here's everything you need to know about what went down on the WTA Tour last week.</p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n</div><h4>Star of the Week</h4>\n<h5>Mirra Andreeva</h5>\n<p>Mirra Andreeva lived up to her billing as the top seed and favorite in Linz, winning her second title of the season and fifth of her career.</p>\n<p>The World No. 9 took care of veterans Sloane Stephens and Sorana Cirstea in her first two matches, then rolled past Elena-Gabriela Ruse in the semifinals. In the final against former champion Anastasia Potapova, the 18-year-old recovered from a rough first set to take the championship match 1-6, 6-4, 6-3. </p>\n<p>This was Andreeva's second career clay title, after winning Iasi in 2024, and she joins Aryna Sabalenka and Jessica Pegula as the only multiple-title winners on tour this year.</p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n        <aside class=\"instagram-post embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--floating embeddable-widget--centered-mobile \"><blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXCT2XejR_e/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\" style=\" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; width:-webkit-calc(100% - 2px); width:calc(100% - 2px);\"><div style=\"padding:16px;\"> <a href=\"htt